0 metres Freestyle, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "4548"} "4 × 200 metres Freestyle Relay, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "4522"} "100 metres Backstroke, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "4535"} "200 metres Breaststroke, Men"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "4476"} "1906"] "\n" [:option {:value "4573"} "1912"] "\n" [:option {:value "4662"} "1920"] "\n" [:option {:value "4741"} "1924"] "\n" [:option {:value "4843"} "1928"] "\n" [:option {:value "4946"} "1932"] "\n" [:option {:value "5037"} "1936"] "\n" [:option {:value "5145"} "1948"] "\n" [:option {:value "5258"} "1952"] "\n" [:option {:value "5390"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "5503"} "1960"] "\n" [:option {:value "5670"} "1964"] "\n" [:option {:value "5878"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "6195"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "6495"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "6765"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "6986"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "7297"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "7654"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "8006"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "8381"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "8786"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "261516"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "322000"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "357025"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19000040"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2001543"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/558"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "400 metres Freestyle, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "13 – 16 July 1908"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/216"} "White City Stadium, London"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/4494"} "25 from 10 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "There was no official world record at this time.  The two favorites were " [:a {:href "/athletes/47414"} "Henry Taylor"] "  and " [:a {:href "/athletes/45155"} "Frank Beaurepaire"] ".  Taylor had won the " [:a {:href "/results/4477"} "mile race"] " and finished 2nd in the " [:a {:href "/results/4476"} "400 metres"] " at the 1906 Athens Olympics.  He had won the Amateur Swimming Association (ASA) title at 440 yards in 1906-1907, but, in 1908, Beaurepaire took the championship.  The defending Olympic champion at this distance was also present, the Austrian " [:a {:href "/athletes/45399"} "Otto Scheff"] ".  The top American swimmer, " [:a {:href "/athletes/51308"} "Charlie Daniels"] ", was entered in this event, but withdrew to save himself for the " [:a {:href "/results/4479"} "shorter distance sprint"] " and the " [:a {:href "/results/4548"} "relay"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the final, Taylor had the fastest start.  After one lap (100 metres in 1:15.0), Taylor, Beaurepaire, and Scheff were in a virtual dead heat.  The 200 metres was passed in 2:35 by Taylor, leading Scheff, who was clocked at 2:37.0.  Beaurepaire then came up quickly and, after 300 metres, he and Taylor were equal at 4:10.0.  But the effort exhausted the Australian, as Taylor drew away to win by at least five yards.  Austria entered a protest in Scheff’s behalf, claiming that he was fouled in the final, but it was disallowed."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47414"} "Henry Taylor"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central